[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1119,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 1158,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155796,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1158,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Juxta-articular myxoma is a benign myxoid tumour morphologically similar to intramuscular/cellular myxoma, arising in the vicinity of large joints.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1120,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 1159,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155797,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1159,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8840/0 Myxoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1121,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1160,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155798,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1160,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E84.Z &amp; XH6Q84 Benign fibrogenic or myofibrogenic tumor, site unknown and Myxoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1122,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155799,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1161,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> periarticular myxoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1123,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155800,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1124,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155801,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Juxta-articular myxoma usually arises adjacent to large joints, with the knee being the most commonly affected site (&gt;&nbsp;85%). Other less commonly affected sites include the hip, shoulder, elbow, and ankle {1592386}; rare locations include the temporomandibular joint {26594976} and hands and feet {15680575}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1125,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155802,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients usually present with swelling or a mass that may be associated with tenderness or pain in the vicinity of large joints. A subset of patients have severe degenerative joint disease or a meniscal tear. The duration of symptoms ranges from weeks to years. On imaging studies, the appearance of a juxta-articular myxoma is similar to that of an intramuscular myxoma {7747183}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1126,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155803,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Juxta-articular myxoma has been described to occur over a wide age range, including rarely in children; however, they typically affect patients in the fifth and sixth decades of life, and nearly three&nbsp;quarters are described in men {1592386; 20157818}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1127,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155804,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In most patients, the etiology is unknown. A minority of patients have a history of degenerative joint disease or trauma, which may be coincidental.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1128,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155805,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1135,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155806,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours usually range in size between 20&nbsp;and 60&nbsp;mm, but tumours as large as 130&nbsp;mm have been described. The cut surface is gelatinous and myxoid, and cystic degeneration is commonly seen {1592386}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1129,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155807,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Juxta-articular myxoma is poorly circumscribed, demonstrating infiltration into the surrounding periarticular soft tissue. The tumour is generally paucicellular and composed of bland spindle-shaped cells with uniform ovoid nuclei, inconspicuous nucleoli, and eosinophilic cytoplasm embedded in a myxoid stroma with few blood vessels. Increased cellularity can be seen (similar to cellular myxoma); however, mitoses are scarce. In the majority of cases, cyst-like spaces lined by a delicate fibrin layer or a thicker layer composed of collagen may be seen. In a subset of cases, haemorrhage, chronic inflammation, and haemosiderin/fibrin deposition may be seen, probably because of trauma. These reactive changes may also be seen in recurrent tumours. Immunohistochemical stains are generally not useful for diagnosis; however, the lesional cells may express CD34 and/or SMA and are negative for S100. Intratumoural muciphages may be detected by histiocyte markers such as CD163.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1130,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155808,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Aspirates show the same features of intramuscular myxoma {33168472}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1131,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155809,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1134,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155810,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> soft tissue around large joints; paucicellular, myxoid, cytologically bland tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1132,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155811,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1133,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155812,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 1172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Local recurrence occurs in as many as one&nbsp;third of patients, sometimes more than once. Malignant transformation does not occur {1592386}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:32:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]